{"name":"Leopard","hex":"#d09800","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Leopard","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Leopard"}],"entries":[{"title":"Leopard","blocks":[{"text":"The leopard is one of the five extant cat species in the genus Panthera. It has a pale yellowish to dark golden fur with dark spots grouped in rosettes. Its body is slender and muscular, reaching a length of 92–183 cm (36–72 in) with a 66–102 cm (26–40 in) long tail and a shoulder height of 60–70 cm (24–28 in). Males typically weigh 30.9–72 kg (68–159 lb), and females 20.5–43 kg (45–95 lb)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/African_leopard_male_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-African_leopard_male_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leopard","wikidata":"Q34706"},{"title":"Leopard pattern","blocks":[{"text":"A leopard pattern is a spotted color pattern, particularly in the hair coat or skin of animals, but can also describe spotting patterns in plants and a distinctive print appearing on clothing and other fabrics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Leopard_%28Panthera_pardus%29.jpg/330px-Leopard_%28Panthera_pardus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leopard_pattern","wikidata":"Q1947255"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Leopard_distribution.jpg/500px-Leopard_distribution.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Leopard_distribution.jpg/500px-Leopard_distribution.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeopard_distribution.jpg"},{"srcset":"https